ve however he begged tony for help  telling him he'd never pass a drug test  when tony saw the baby seat for  christopher's infant daughter pierced by  a huge branch he realized that  christopher was way too much of a loose  cannon as an addict he was also  vulnerable to being flipped by the fence  instead of helping christopher tony  pinched his nephew's nose and suffocated  him as with many of the show's  characters it was a pathetic ending for  a cruel sad life even the show's major  characters weren't immune he died in the  season six episode kennedy and heidi how  are you doing  stuff  yeah  bobby baccalieri was the closest thing  to a decent human being on the sopranos  you're not going to jump me  what  i'm hoping here i'll have to king you  ridiculed for his weight and gentle  manner he nonetheless was highly loyal  to junior soprano and then tony when he  became part of his crew bobby was born  into this life thanks to his dad who was  a ruthless hitman bobby managed to avoid  killing for most of his career making  money as a loan shark he didn't live the  kind of fast-paced lifestyle of the rest  of the crew and didn't even keep a  mistress that changed after he married  tony's sister janice bobby's longtime  wife karen died in a car accident and  janice insinuated her way into his life  and that of his kids when tony and his  wife carmelo went on a cabin excursion  with bobby and janice bobby got in a  fistfight with tony and juan defending  his wife's honor tony resented losing  and gave bobby his first hit assignment  much to bobby chagrin when phil leotardo  decided to wipe out tony's mob bobby was  one of the targets in the season six  episode the blue comet poor bobby was  shot down in a public hit in a model  railroad store it was a sad end for a  man who probably would have had a  different career if he hadn't been born  into this one  phil leotardo was another mobster who  was released from prison during the  course of the show he served a 20-year  sentence and went back to work for the  libertatsi family and johnny sack  leotardo had a veneer of respectability  but he was a brutal killer and sickening  homophobe he nearly started wars with  tony soprano several times over various  offenses related to business and his men  getting killed or beaten that included  him wanting to kill tony's cousin tony  blandetto and one of tony's soldiers  vito spadafor  after yet another conflict leotardo got  the go-ahead to kill tony and his top  men after tony evaded him he negotiated  with leotardo's disgruntled captains and  got their permission to kill him  leotardo was the last on-screen death of  the entire series occurring during the  series finale made in america tony's men  spotted him at a gas station and shot  him with the car running and his  grandkids sitting in the back seat  what made the scene particularly  horrifying was that the car lurched  forward and crushed leotardo's skull  rendering him unrecognizable check out  one of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite stuff are coming soon subscribe  to our youtube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

